10ay|v|To make to be the same; to unite or combine in such a manner as to make one; to treat as being one or having the same purpose or effect; to consider as the same in any relation. ; To establish the identity of; to prove to be the same with something described, claimed, or asserted; as, to identify stolen property. ; To become the same; to coalesce in interest, purpose, use, effect, etc.	s:apg,19,2~apg,19,2	d:g8p,38,4;deo,32,3;ndx,30,3~g8p,38,4;ndx,30,3;deo,32,3	D:2ana,0,4~2ana,0,4
